      ],
      "owner": "Individual player root DisabledHearths ListTag of Pos long + Level ResourceLocation strings; client set uses Pair<BlockPos, ResourceLocation>. This is preference data, not protective status or temperature authority.",
      "chain": [
        "Screen toggle changes client set; removal of arbitrary HashSet first element above 64 bounds GUI path only. onClose sends entire list only if this screen boolean differs from entry value.",
        "Registered packet7 has server sender/reception-side gate and enqueues persistentData.merge(message.nbt); no key whitelist, list limit, coordinate validation or menu validity in this handler. This is source-level authority limitation, no exploit execution.",
        "Clone server handler transfers exact ListTag reference for both death and nondeath; no copy and no isWasDeath filter.",
        "Server EntityJoinLevel handler sends only DisabledHearths to that player; receiving client clears and rebuilds its static set. Join is broader than login.",
        "Hearth periodic client predicate checks typed position+dimension pair; actual air-particle method requires showParticles. No server damage/immunity effect is granted by this preference."
      ],
      "limits": [
        "Shared old/new ListTag alias is not detached Clone ownership. Do not transplant this into Dynasty permanent root transfer.",
        "64 entries limit is solely client toggle path, not server or reader validation; malformed ResourceLocation may throw and null packet NBT is not handled here.",
        "No logout reset found in direct DISABLED_HEARTHS mutators; replacement-on-join packet clears state, but no connection/epoch marker in packet. No runtime cross-server replay claim.",
        "Debug renderer compares Pair<BlockPos,String> with set of Pair<BlockPos,ResourceLocation>; this secondary predicate does not use same key type. No complete renderer/runtime validation claimed.",
        "Turning hide on then off can evict another entry while local boolean returns to old value, so onClose may skip persisting the changed set. Static edge case, not native reproduction.",
        "No independent disk codec here: player root persistence is underlying Forge responsibility, not newly verified by this chain."
      ],
      "dedup": {
        "existing_exact_symbol_matches": [],
        "contrast": "Prior 09a250b118eb29c97025 owns temperature capability traits/modifiers/permanent attribute whitelist. This owns per-player visual preferences by dimension+position and restores a client preference set. One whole preference lifecycle only, no separate count for GUI, packet, serializer or Clone callback.",
        "unresolved": "Exact-symbol absence is not full semantic uniqueness. Coordinator must compare all preference owner families and scope; immune scope excludes this case."
      }
    },
    {
